Vendored from: https://github.com/humayunk1/PKC (ParK() in pkc.c)
Commit: 91b78f443b47c2e339cabf480f786a530a61a9f1

Changes w.r.t. upstream pkc.c:
- Graph loader reads our .bin (CSR) format and copies offsets/edges as-is in parallel
  (load_graph_from_binary). Adjacency lists in the .bin files are already sorted, so no sorting.
- eid_t (edge offsets) is 64-bit (upstream: unsigned int), so graphs with more than 2^32 edges load.
- ParK() allocates and returns the core-number array, so the timed region includes the output
  allocation, as for the other implementations.
- curr/next buffers keep the upstream size (n).
